{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Desire","html":"<article id='sn1.69'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Saṁyutta Nikāya 1.69 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Linked Discourses 1.69 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>7. Addhavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>7. Overcome </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Icchāsutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Desire </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Kenassu bajjhatī loko, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“What is it that binds the world? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kissa vinayāya muccati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>By removing what is it freed? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kissassu vippahānena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>With the giving up of what </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sabbaṁ chindati bandhanan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>are all bonds severed?” </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Icchāya bajjhatī loko, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Desire is what binds the world. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>icchāvinayāya muccati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>By the removing of desire it’s freed. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Icchāya vippahānena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>With the giving up of desire, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sabbaṁ chindati bandhanan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>all bonds are severed.” </span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
